# vLLM v0.26.0 patch 05/18 (apply after the four DeepSeek-V4 patches above it).
#
# DeepSeek-V4 on ROCm: mHC on TileLang with one pre-norm GEMM kernel under BI.
#
# Under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1, MHCPreOp / MHCPostOp do not use AITER's
# mhc_pre / mhc_post (which split their reductions by token count), and
# _tilelang_hc_prenorm_gemm always uses one kernel instead of choosing one of
# three by token count. Raises instead of silently falling back if TileLang mHC
# is unavailable.
#
# Why BI needs it: the same row got different post/comb mixes (~3e-7) in
# different batches, and a decode token differed from the same token in a
# prefill.
#
# Upstream: not yet proposed. Main replaced the TileLang mHC kernels and added
# AITER fused/delayed mHC; part of the DeepSeek-V4 ROCm RFC.
#
# Source commits:
#   [ROCm][DSv4][BI] mHC on TileLang with one pre-norm GEMM kernel under BI
#
